# Cursor AI Rules — Nectar Enviro Ops Console

## 1. Project Reference & Navigation
- Always read and follow the master guidelines in `.agents/AGENTS.md`.
- Consult `.agents/planning/CODEBASE_MAP.md` as the primary reference map before running searches across the codebase.
- Use Section 2 ("Fast-Lookup Decision Matrix") in `CODEBASE_MAP.md` to directly locate target pages, components, and state stores.

## 2. Command: /update-agents
When the user types `/update-agents`:
- Scan `client/app/`, `client/components/`, and `client/lib/` for any new or modified files.
- Synchronize `.agents/planning/CODEBASE_MAP.md` to reflect new pages, components, state stores, and lookup entries.
- Summarize the updates made to the map.

## 3. Tech Stack & Conventions
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript.
- **UI & Design**: Ant Design 6.6, Tailwind CSS v4, brand navy `#1C4463` (tokens in `client/lib/theme.ts`).
- **Data**: NestJS API via `client/lib/api/*`; domain stores in `client/lib/*/store.ts` (`shift`, `leave`, `ot-decision`, `safety`, `e-permit`, `training`, …) cache in `localStorage`.
- **i18n**: English / Hindi / Marathi — every UI string goes through `client/lib/i18n/`.
- **Access Control**: `client/lib/rbac.ts`. HoD (Senior Manager) = Plant Manager access across all plants; use `isManagerRole()`.
